    {
      "bbox": [
        517,
        707,
        1981,
        1255
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Most of these people work on a 9 to 5 schedule. Why? Largely because it's always been done that way. Just traditional. The result is brutal congestion twice a day on the transportation facilities. The subways, highways, railroads, buses, ferries and every other mode of getting to and from work are overtaxed within the narrow time bands of morning and evening rush hours. At other times of day, even as little as 30 minutes outside these peak hours, the facilities are much less heavily traveled.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.4569,
          "min": -1.9672
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 109,
          "mean": -0.0021,
          "min": -0.0876
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 12416,
        "area_px": 806108,
        "density": 0.0154,
        "chars": 497,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 40.03
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        543,
        1195,
        2018,
        1502
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Every one of these travelers knows the discomfort and irritation in such human concentration. Time is wasted; most of the transit delays occur in the peak periods. Workers arrive late at their offices, people's spirits sag, efficiency is impaired.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.3958,
          "min": -1.9575
        },
        "category": {
